 {:seon.task/name "process-tests-run-from-inside"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner's ruling, 2026-11-10 (docs/decisions.md): tests run inside Seon. Test plan step 3 (notes test-system-plan-2026-11-10.md, its fallback first). Today an agent's process tests are deferred to the gate (seon.agent/run-selection: a child forked from an agent has no process store), and the gate (seon.fx/run-on-checkout) makes a git worktree and runs bin/test in it: select, seed, maybe build (a one-test gate 29 s after step 3a; 231 tests 4.5-5 min in a real done). Plan: the agent's test child runs its process tests; their roots are exec'd from the running binary on a main branched at the candidate's commit in the one store (Datahike branch! from a commit beside seon.db/open-main!), with no source root, so their boot imports nothing over it (seon.test-store/shared-root! passes the checkout as source root today: that goes for these roots). REPL experiments first, on a worktree root of its own on a fresh store: a main branched at a commit; a root on it holding that branch's program (a deleted var unmapped, a changed macro's callers reloaded); a process test run from an agent's child against it. Removes in the same landing: run-on-checkout's worktree and bin/test call for every run but the full run, the process store's seed (seon.test-store/process-store, make-process-store!, bin/root seed in bin/test), the deferral in run-selection. Proofs to write: a-done-builds-nothing (a candidate reaching no root-side code makes zero builds and no worktree, at 10 and 100 process tests reached); a root-side candidate's process tests run on a built binary. Estimate: a gate is a boot (0.25 s), a first fork, and the tests' own work."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}]
